    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1036-a1">

                <pb facs="1007" n="841" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg841"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ministry of Foreign Affairs to the American Embassy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 3, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to note No. 1532 of April 2, the Royal Ministry of Foreign Affairs is
                    sorry to have to communicate to the Embassy of the United States of America that
                    the competent military authorities can not comply with the desire expressed by
                    the relatives of the soldier Orocchi Giuseppe that he be transferred from the
                    artillery to a sanitary or hospital corps, the present laws in force preventing
                    such a change.</p>
                <p>The Embassy will please find attached a copy of the note received from the R.
                    Ministry of War on the subject.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
